00:11:22.007 --> 00:11:23.758
You see when I got out that life,

00:11:23.758 --> 00:11:26.273
I cleaned my life for a minute there.

00:11:26.273 --> 00:11:29.484
I was able to pick up my guitar

00:11:29.484 --> 00:11:31.494
and play the blues.

00:11:31.494 --> 00:11:34.535
You know I put a record out there now,

00:11:34.535 --> 00:11:37.202
that's number five in the world.

00:11:38.363 --> 00:11:41.377
And then I got all kinds
of awards, inducted

00:11:41.377 --> 00:11:45.965
in the blues hall of
fame, B.B. King, you know?

00:11:45.965 --> 00:11:49.715
So, I was successful in
the game 150 trophies

00:11:51.013 --> 00:11:54.047
as the godfather in the game and in the

00:11:54.047 --> 00:11:56.114
hall of fame in the music.

00:11:56.114 --> 00:11:59.210
So, that's why my book says, "Blues man,

00:11:59.210 --> 00:12:01.591
Michael G. Fillmore Slim, high-talk

00:12:01.591 --> 00:12:04.528
of the stage and the streets."

00:12:04.528 --> 00:12:05.647
- [Mark Lait] What personality trait

00:12:05.647 --> 00:12:06.961
helped you most as a pimp?

00:12:06.961 --> 00:12:08.949
- [Fillmore Slim] What personality?

00:12:08.949 --> 00:12:13.182
Well, I've always been
a ladies man, you know

00:12:13.182 --> 00:12:17.182
I always was a charmer.
I could charm any chick.

00:12:18.684 --> 00:12:21.357
I could stop any chick. I'll tell you

00:12:21.357 --> 00:12:25.524
a story, I remember I went
by the Chinese theater,

00:12:27.377 --> 00:12:30.762
I just came back and I
seen this Caucasian lady

00:12:30.762 --> 00:12:34.929
all dressed in white,
walking down sunset, okay?

00:12:34.929 --> 00:12:37.597
No, Hollywood Boulevard
right by the Chinese,

00:12:37.597 --> 00:12:39.561
and I stopped the car and went around this

00:12:39.561 --> 00:12:41.067
little alley right there, you know

00:12:41.067 --> 00:12:43.661
before you get to the Chinese theater,

00:12:43.661 --> 00:12:46.057
so I came around just so she crossed

00:12:46.057 --> 00:12:48.427
that alley, I pull up, I blocked her

00:12:48.427 --> 00:12:50.273
I said, "Baby." She said, "What?"

00:12:50.273 --> 00:12:53.089
I said, "Here's your
car, this is your car."

00:12:53.089 --> 00:12:54.387
She said, "What you mean?" I said,

00:12:54.387 --> 00:12:56.508
"It's all white, red inside, this

00:12:56.508 --> 00:12:59.756
car came for you." And
she was so fascinated.

00:12:59.756 --> 00:13:01.747
I said, "Get in." Spin around, she got

00:13:01.747 --> 00:13:04.296
in the car, come to find out we rode

00:13:04.296 --> 00:13:06.641
and talk, come to find out she was

00:13:06.641 --> 00:13:09.322
O.J. Reynolds. Tobacco king, it was

00:13:09.322 --> 00:13:10.822
his granddaughter.

00:13:12.096 --> 00:13:15.370
You know and we talked and when I find

00:13:15.370 --> 00:13:17.167
that out, you know I told her to have

00:13:17.167 --> 00:13:18.084
a good day.

00:13:19.995 --> 00:13:20.828
